  <div><h4>Math</h4><ul><li>Word problems use the class routine: circle the numbers, underline the question, label T (total), g (groups), and e (each), use the T-g-e triangle to choose multiply or divide, then solve with a tape diagram</li><li>Skip counting fills the tape diagram box by box, like the class worksheet</li><li>Skip count cards and Times Table Trophies: one number at a time, bronze (build the card), silver (mixed facts), gold (multiply and divide), then a diploma</li><li>Fact Blaster for mixed review, with arrays and fact strategies; missed facts come back</li><li>Place value and fractions with charts, number lines, and pictures</li><li>Number Lab (her Starbase missions): Groups · Each · Total rescue kits with a triangle and tape diagram, a skip-count trail, times-table trails 2–12 with arrays and equal groups for multiplying and dividing, place value, and fraction bars. She picks the track and the size of the numbers.</li><li>No timers anywhere</li></ul></div>
